{title: Filled With The Spirit}
{subtitle: Exodus 31:1–5; 31:6; 31:7–11; 35:30–35; 36:1–2; 37:1–9}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [C] | [Bb] | ×2
| [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I have called [C]by name Bezalel son [Bb]of Uri
From the tribe [Dm]of Judah he stands before me
I have [C]filled him with the Spirit of [Bb]God
With skill and understanding to [Dm]build His house
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Designing works in gold [C]and silver and bronze
[Bb]Cutting stones and carving wood with [Dm]grace
In every kind of craft [C]the wisdom flows
To [Bb]make the sanctuary as I com[Dm]mand
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I have ap[C]pointed Oholiab to work [Bb]with him
From the tribe [Dm]of Dan they share the call
I have given [C]skill to every craftsman
[Bb]So they can make what I have com[Dm]manded
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
The tent of meeting and the ark [C]of testimony
[Bb]The atonement cov[Dm]er on top of it all
The table and [C]the lampstand and the altar
Wo[Bb]ven garments for Aaron to [Dm]serve as priest
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Moses told the people [C]what the Lord had said
[Bb]Bezalel was filled [Dm]with skill and knowledge
He made the ark of [C]acacia wood
[Bb]Overlaid with pure gold inside and [Dm]out
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Mercy seat of gold with [C]cherubim
[Bb]Wings spread upward over[Dm]shadowing the place
Facing each other in the ho[C]ly spot
[Bb]Just as the Lord had commanded them to [Dm]make
{end_of_verse}
